Translation patch: <&MontgomeryPoint as Mul<&Scalar>>::mul, and deletes Scalar::bits_le

Change: `self.mul_bits_be(scalar.bits_le().rev().skip(1))` is replaced by the body of `mul_bits_be`,
looping over bit indices 254..=0 with `cur_bit = ((bytes[i >> 3] >> (i & 7)) & 1) == 1`;
parameter `scalar` renamed to `s`. `bits_le` (now unused, `pub(crate)`) is deleted.
Original `mul_bits_be` loop, for comparison:
    for cur_bit in bits {
        let choice: u8 = (prev_bit ^ cur_bit) as u8;
        debug_assert!(choice == 0 || choice == 1);
        ProjectivePoint::conditional_swap(&mut x0, &mut x1, choice.into());
        differential_add_and_double(&mut x0, &mut x1, &affine_u);
        prev_bit = cur_bit;
    }
Why: Aeneas only models `Iterator::next` (aeneas#1057). The rename: a variable named `scalar` clashes with the `scalar` module in Lean (aeneas#1098).
Behaviour: identical: `bits_le().rev().skip(1)` yields bits 254..=0, the same order and formula.
Relies on: `Scalar::as_bytes` returns `&self.bytes`.

